                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f71856d5-406c-3969-8481-a954527fe6be",
                        "entry_id": "95b3796a-1509-3af5-a3b3-9dee8ca7ff6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A man, a chap, a guy; especially a Hispanic or Spanish man."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39cd8746-5dc4-430c-86db-d76349ee8981",
                                "sense_id": "f71856d5-406c-3969-8481-a954527fe6be",
                                "text": "[W]e're glad to learn that the Yankee bullet has not quite stopped your breath. You're all right, hombre!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c62c7fed-f838-4913-8f9d-a420050e83fb",
                                "sense_id": "f71856d5-406c-3969-8481-a954527fe6be",
                                "text": "That hombre now with the worn out hat, tattered shirt, and fragmentary breeches, wears a sword. Bless you, his dignity would suffer greatly without it!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "85c2a588-3ea4-4562-ac6f-7e2fe9c0177d",
                                "sense_id": "f71856d5-406c-3969-8481-a954527fe6be",
                                "text": "Coming towards us was the biggest, meanest looking hombre I'd ever seen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8a3ada0-0fc5-47db-a9cd-3f69638c904e",
                                "sense_id": "f71856d5-406c-3969-8481-a954527fe6be",
                                "text": "The foreman. As tough an hombre who ever lived. If Mr. Bell had sent Jackson instead of me, he'd take your rifle and beat you half to death with it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff2c27fb-1d84-4b51-a42a-693570e3f187",
                                "sense_id": "f71856d5-406c-3969-8481-a954527fe6be",
                                "text": "There was a pause I didn't like, punctuated by shrieks of shrill laughter from the hombres at the bar. Only Mexicans can laugh like that."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
